From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:09:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: one exit-drain deadline per file

Review (claude-compiler): file teardown drained each VM with its own
120 s cap, so several VMs that keep retiring could hold an
uninterruptible exit for N x 120 s. The cap is now an explicit
g16_drain::Clock argument, and the exit path gives every VM what is left
of one per-file deadline. Other drains keep CAP_MS each. Host tests cover
a cap below the budget, an exhausted deadline and four progressing VMs
sharing one deadline.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
